✅ Basic Concept Questions
1.	Q: What is Prim’s Algorithm?
A: Prim’s Algorithm is a greedy algorithm that finds the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) for a connected weighted graph. It starts from a vertex and continuously adds the smallest possible edge that connects a new vertex to the tree.
2.	Q: What is a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST)?
A: MST is a subset of the edges of a connected, weighted graph that connects all vertices with the minimum possible total edge weight and without any cycles.
3.	Q: What is the time complexity of Prim’s Algorithm?
A:
o	Using an adjacency matrix and a linear search (minKey): O(V²)
o	Using a priority queue with adjacency list: O(E log V) (more efficient)
